The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when an application exposes a reference to an internal object, such as a file or database record, without proper authorization checks. In the provided API, the filename is taken directly from user input without validating whether the user has permission to access that specific file. This could allow an attacker to manipulate the filename parameter to access unauthorized files on the server, leading to potential data exposure or unauthorized access to sensitive information.

